given above?" 13194139535974 false] [17592186377532 1017 #edb/ref 17592186377533 13194139535974 true] [17592186377532 1089 "q-16548" 13194139535974 true] [17592186377532 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535974 true] [17592186377532 1100 "For the ellipse \n$\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{5}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{2}=1$, find the lengths of its major and minor axes." 13194139535974 true] [17592186377532 1113 #uuid "9ff8c2aa-59f0-5520-88ff-40444c85393f" 13194139535974 true] [17592186377532 1145 "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=-4$ and $k=3,$ so the center is located at $(-4,3).$\n\nIn the given equation, we also have ${a}^{2}=5$ and ${b}^{2}=2.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=5,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{5}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=2,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=\\sqrt{5},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\sqrt{5}=2\\sqrt{5},$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\sqrt{2}=2\\sqrt{2}.$" 13194139535974 true] [17592186377533 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377534 13194139535974 true] [17592186377533 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377535 13194139535974 true] [17592186377533 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377536 13194139535974 true] [17592186377533 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377537 13194139535974 true] [17592186377533 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377538 13194139535974 true] [17592186377533 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535974 true] [17592186377533 1041 "selection" 13194139535974 true] [17592186377533 1104 #edb/ref 17592186377535 13194139535974 true] [17592186377533 1110 #uuid "0d149ec3-1bda-5a45-85df-69addf9bf489" 13194139535974 true] [17592186377534 1034 "$2\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\sqrt{2}$" 13194139535974 true] [17592186377534 1103 #edb